{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1303051-dark-eras-byzantine\u2019s-empire-kindred","id":1303051,"title":"[Dark Eras] Byzantine\u2019s Empire Kindred","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-04-06T05:12:01-07:00","id":1303051,"title":"[Dark Eras] Byzantine\u2019s Empire Kindred","content":"As I (finally) coming close to running my crossover plots in <b>Werewolf/Contagion Chronicle </b>circa year 800, and as moving action to the Constantinople \u2013 I need more information on the Kindred society in them around 7<sup>th</sup> till 10<sup>th</sup> century \u2013 or invent fan stuff for it. We have <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1137216-dark-eras-fan-byzantine-empire\">long general topic for crossover fan Dark Era in East Roman Empire</a> \u2013 but I need info strictly about Kindred. I read <b>Vampire the Requiem</b> corebook 2E,<b> Ancient Mysteries</b> and <b>Fall of Camarilla</b> appendix about Byzantium and know this info from those:<ul><li>Lancea et Sanctum at the start of 6th century is de facto ruling society of Kindred in East Roman Empire.</li> <li>LeS is enforcing Traditions as we know it. Church Ethernal on East is also spreading it\u2019s dogma of separating worships of mortals from that of Kindred.</li> <li>LeS rules using first Prisci Council, with Clan leaders and LeS Patriatch siting in it, where Patriatch is ruling council \u2018morally\u2019 from it. There is official seat for the defunct Senex, but it\u2019s vacant then.</li> <li>In 4th till 6th century Legio Mortuum is evolving into Legion of Damned, de facto military faction inside of LeS. But LoD works more or less like LM before it.</li> <li>Cult of Argurs was banned in Byzantium in year 370. That means there is no canon \u2018pagan\u2019 faction from <b>Fall of Camarilla</b>, at least till 10<sup>th</sup> century ( see later ). I wonder if Mother of Bones cannot replace them from 6<sup>th</sup> century. ( Will return to this later on. )</li> <li>Peregrine Collegia is de facto destroyed with the fall of Camarilla. Faction never truly recovered, leading just to becoming Unaligned bands in Byzantium.</li> <li>Great test of strength of new political dynamics was <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Plague_of_Justinian\" target=\"_blank\">Plague of Justinian</a> in 541 AD. Vampires were starving when humans lay dead en masse. Now it\u2019s also part of <b>CoD</b> canon, as creation event of <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/the-jeremiad-contagion-chronicle/\" target=\"_blank\">Jeremiad Sworn</a> against Contagion ( that is suspected to be spread by the 541 AD Plague ).</li> <li><b>Ancient Mysteries</b> is pointing that Camarilla in Byzantium survived until 1095 as <i>Adamantes Athanatoi</i> - the Unconquered Immortals - Easter Roman Empire off-shoot of\u2026 Senex? Secular Legio Mortuum? Details are not so important, cause it\u2019s structure is clearly inspired by human <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Immortals_(Byzantine_Empire)\" target=\"_blank\">Athanatoi</a>, special unit of aristocracy army that also being governors of Byzantium provinces.</li> <li>It seems that <b>Ancient Mysteries</b> in Crusades Flashpoint are implying that Circle of Crone was created in late Middle Ages. I must say I much more like this idea of CoC creation than late 19<sup>th</sup> century one in Scotland from <b>VtR</b> 2E. \u2018Through such discussions it was decided that the cults would band together for their continued survival, forming a protective orbit against their enemies. Many of these cults called on mother figures to protect them and to bring an end to their enemies. By the rise of <i>Das Heiligen Nacht Reich</i>, this combined Kindred front was known as the Circle of the Crone and was considered anathema in most god-fearing domains.\u2019</li> <li>And there it\u2019s small numbers of pagan vampires in famous <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Varangian_Guard\" target=\"_blank\">Varangian Guard</a>, in Vikings bodyguards of human Emperor from late 10<sup>th</sup> century: \u2018Ironically, one of the largest unmolested populations of Circle cultists existed in the heart of Christendom, Constantinople. The Imperator allowed occasional nomadic Kindred from northern Europe and similarly barbaric lands to remain within the city so long as they demonstrated a strong capacity for combat and were willing to serve. This <i>Tagma ton Xenon</i> (\u201cForeign Guard\u201d) protected the Kindred of the city in exchange for feeding rights among the city\u2019s non-Greek population and a small amount of coin from the Imperator\u2019s coffers. While each member of the Guard was baptized upon induction, the Sanctified largely left the warriors to their own devices, only chastising them for their worship if they behaved in a manner deemed disruptive to the larger population.\u2019</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-06T05:14:31-07:00","id":1303052,"title":"","content":"Those were canon information from books. Here are my fan wonderings and musings on this Dark Eras stuff.<ul><li>In <b>VtR</b> 2E corebook setting of Athenes ( Polis of Erabus ) is mentioning of chtonics gods vampiric priestess <i>Despoina,</i> <i>Mother of Bones</i>. She worship Echidna, mythological Mother of Monsters, so works as cult for proto-Circle of Crone in area. I would even more gladly use here, as I wanted to use some beasts crossovers \u2013 and worshipping Mother of Monsters certainly works here. 8-) So I would probably use Cult of Echidna as proto-Circle of Crone in setting, replacing Cult of Augurs, centuries before great unification. As I use Sworn from <b>Contagion Chronicle</b>, this cult will join probably <i>Omphalos</i>, predecessor to Rosetta Society, in place of CoC.</li> <li><i>Athanatoi</i>, as particular human unit idea, was created in year 970 AD. However, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Theme_(Byzantine_district)\" target=\"_blank\">Themata Refrom</a>, where Byzantium was divided between between military-administrative provinces \u2013 was done in 640s and spread as idea around Empire. By 700s it was popular model or ruling in Byzantium. By 750s there was created <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tagma_(military)\" target=\"_blank\">Tagma</a> military units around Empire, that were de facto long arm of Emperor. I think that creation of <i>Adamantes Athanatoi </i>as Kindred Covenant on late 690s /early 700s is okay in that context.</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-07T20:03:15-07:00","id":1303464,"title":"","content":"I like this a lot! I feel like it would be interesting to have a nascent Invictus replace the Legion of the Damned.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24708-spectre9924","name":"Spectre9924","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24708_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-07T21:49:58-07:00","id":1303473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spectre9924</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1303051-dark-eras-byzantine\u2019s-empire-kindred?p=1303464#post1303464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like this a lot! I feel like it would be interesting to have a nascent Invictus replace the Legion of the Damned.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the end - it will be. Legion of Damned is radical fanatics 'knight order' ( based on real world historical radical Christian groups of 3rd till 6th century). Where Athanatoi are combaining (future) Invictus administrator and noble side with literal generals and army of Empire ( see Themata system of ruling). In coming centuries, Legion of Damned from slowly separate Covenant become simply large faction in Byzantine Lancea Sanctum. Rest of more secular knights become part of more militant Athanatoi arms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 10-31-2019, 11:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-08T05:51:36-07:00","id":1303504,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1437_5.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1437\" data-vbnamecard=\"1437\">wyrdhamster</a> I'd like to call your attention to a missing piece of the Roman puzzle, which I've <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1187238-unique-benefits-for-the-peregrine-collegia-and-legio-mortuum?p=1187639#post1187639\">touched on in another post and document link (Cursus Mortuis)</a>. <br /> <br /> In any event, the Legion of the Damned is, paradoxically, one of the weakest Covenants of Rome from a mechanical standpoint. They offer the ability to learn weapon styles half-off and... that's it. So you join and in exchange for cutting yourself out of other power factions you get an XP cut. <br /> <br /> What they turn into is more interesting: you get part of them joining the Lancea as it rises in prominence and control. You get part of them joining the Invictus--which makes sense since the Legio would be utterly infested with Mithraic adherents, whose oath-focus is carried into the Invictus.<br /> <br /> Yet the Legio was probably more important in the East than the west, where barbarians pushed them to the sidelines and gave local Kindred other options for mercenaries. So the progression in Byzantine would follow as you've indicated: districts and noble factions under Athanatoi administrators around a core of Lancea control brought in by Constantine. On that point, the Senex probably let them have &quot;Constantinople&quot; as it 1. wasn't Rome, and 2. drew a lot of Lancea-aligned vamps out and away from Rome. They still thought their Rome was all that, even after the political capital shifted to Ravenna. How cute.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-08T16:55:29-07:00","id":1303656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1303051-dark-eras-byzantine\u2019s-empire-kindred?p=1303504#post1303504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What they turn into is more interesting: you get part of them joining the Lancea as it rises in prominence and control. You get part of them joining the Invictus--which makes sense since the Legio would be utterly infested with Mithraic adherents, whose oath-focus is carried into the Invictus.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nitpicking, but Legio Mortuum joined not Invictus, but <i>Athanatoi </i>- even when Athanatoi, practiclly, is predecesor of Invictus ( and use most of mechanics for it ) - Athanatoi are <i>much</i> more militaristic in day to day outlook. Simply because they are composed of noble-soldiers intermixing groups and factions. ( See Themata province system. ) <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1303051-dark-eras-byzantine\u2019s-empire-kindred?p=1303504#post1303504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So the progression in Byzantine would follow as you've indicated: districts and noble factions under Athanatoi administrators around a core of Lancea control brought in by Constantine.</div> </div> </div> </div>Trying to understand this statemant - you mean that Legio Mortuum split in half? With first half becoming Legion of Damned, under Lancea Sanctum, and second creating Athanatoi? I get it right?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1303051-dark-eras-byzantine\u2019s-empire-kindred?p=1303504#post1303504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On that point, the Senex probably let them have &quot;Constantinople&quot; as it 1. wasn't Rome, and 2. drew a lot of Lancea-aligned vamps out and away from Rome. They still thought their Rome was all that, even after the political capital shifted to Ravenna. How cute.</div> </div> </div> </div>Senex in canon material is pointed as blind to the fall of Rome and danger of Strix. And Byzantine Kindred society is build on the rebellion against words of Senex. Then, yes, it's that Senex thought 'let them those... Longinians.... have this Constantinopole - and we will have our glorious Rome'. Well, even ancient vampires can wrong bet. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-08T19:45:37-07:00","id":1303696,"title":"","content":"The Legion of the Dead/Grim Battalion presented in the 2e core book offers a mercenary offshoot of Legio Mortuum that could very realistically have had numerous pagans in their ranks in secret.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24708-spectre9924","name":"Spectre9924","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24708_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-09T19:27:39-07:00","id":1303864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1303051-dark-eras-byzantine\u2019s-empire-kindred?p=1303656#post1303656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nitpicking, but Legio Mortuum joined not Invictus, but <i>Athanatoi </i>- even when Athanatoi, practiclly, is predecesor of Invictus ( and use most of mechanics for it ) - Athanatoi are <i>much</i> more militaristic in day to day outlook. Simply because they are composed of noble-soldiers intermixing groups and factions. ( See Themata province system. )</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, fair enough. Invictus penetrated Byzantium later--much later--thanks to the strength of the Lancea there. I was thinking more holistically, however, and it was in the Western Empire that the Legio found allies in the young Invictus movement. <br /> <br /> Caveat: as best we can tell.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Trying to understand this statemant - you mean that Legio Mortuum split in half? With first half becoming Legion of Damned, under Lancea Sanctum, and second creating Athanatoi? I get it right? </div> </div> </div>The Legio disintegrated as a Covenant entity over time. Its purpose was the militant enforcement and guard arm of the Senex. Without the Senex they were just organized thugs, and found new purpose elsewhere. Gallows Post are a group that are hinted at descending from them, as well as various mercenary factions, Legion of the Damned, etc. You could have a lot of fun tracing the misadventures of the Legio through Europe's spasm of violence. I suspect that any last shred of their identity as Legio vanished when Constantinople fell to the Turks. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Senex in canon material is pointed as blind to the fall of Rome and danger of Strix. And Byzantine Kindred society is build on the rebellion against words of Senex. Then, yes, it's that Senex thought 'let them those... Longinians.... have this Constantinopole - and we will have our glorious Rome'. Well, even ancient vampires can wrong bet. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> </div> </div> </div>Vampires ruin everything. <b><i>Especially</i></b> their own clever institutions.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-01T01:13:04-07:00","id":1309137,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Athantoi Covenant ( fan version )</span></b><br /> Themata province system was created in the mid-7th century in the aftermath of the Slavic invasion of the Balkans and Muslim conquests of parts of Byzantine territory. It overturned older Roman system the strict division of civil and military offices. With new ruling system forming on their eyes, disciples of Ayzebel from Cathage went for power and to control Plague, for the good of Empire. New group stated they want to stable society and give victories with Contagion for the Byzantium. They become nation sensitive leaders monsters. At the dawn of year 700s. they called themselves <i>Athanatoi</i>, Immortals. New Sworn were created in Byzantium.<br /> <br /> <i>Athanatoi</i> Covenant of vampires is rising sect, building on the remnants of Senex that was powerful only 3 centuries earlier. They are following the Oaths of various <i>Strategoi </i>to <i>Dominus Noctis Imperator</i> ruled over a council of <i>Prisci</i>, the eldest members of each Kindred clan. Reconnecting old infrastructures of crumbled Senex to new conspiracy under Night Emperor, they usher new Vampiric Empire inside Easter Roman Empire, with moral support of Sanctified. Set on the idea of feudalism and securing the stability of Both Empires, after centuries of unrest in lands, many neonates are flocking to the new faction \u2013 counting also on the power and influence in coming centuries.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-02T15:44:38-07:00","id":1309528,"title":"","content":"An NPC from the Era, I create for <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1303812-contagion-plauges-of-history-origins-of-sworn?p=1309526#post1309526\">my interpretation of Plague of Justinian as Contagion event</a>...<br /> <br /> <b><i>Christophoros Diogenus</i></b> \u2013 Vampire \u2013 Venture Legion of Damned ( Lancea Sanctum ) \u2013 Sworn: Jeremiad \u2013 Christophoros was one of leading generals in East Roman Empire wars with Arabs. When he was finally pierced on the battlefield by the blade of unfaithful, he started his descent from the world of the living. Seeing merits in his devotion and strategy skills, he was Embraced by his vampiric sire, in his tent, barely living. He quickly returned to the Army of the Night, fighting in the Longinus name. Now, fighting with the heretics, Chirstophoros found out that dead do not stand dead long enough \u2013 and some of the killed are returning to unlife, to fight them once again. Diogenus started campaign against those undead, in the name of God and Unholy Emperor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T08:29:23-07:00","id":1344949,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Monsters Society, p. 2 \u2013 Members of Sworn</b></span><br /> <br /> Here is list of basic NPCs concepts filling Sworn numbers from my proposed <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1344875-dark-eras-fan-constantinople-%E2%80%93-early-medieval-istanbul-turkey-%E2%80%93-700-%E2%80%93-1000-ad\">Constantinople fan setting</a>. I put design comments in \u2018//\u2019 marks. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12493_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12493\" data-vbnamecard=\"12493\">Khanwulf</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24708-spectre9924\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24708_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24708\" data-vbnamecard=\"24708\">Spectre9924</a> - You maybe interested in those. Any help with my unsure options on '???' ?<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Jeremiad</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>Iovinus \u2013 Archbishop of Constantinople ( called Patriarch )</b><br /> <br /> <b>Clan</b>: Daeva<br /> <b>Covenant:</b> Ag\u00eda Lans ( gr. Lancea Sanctum )<br /> Iovinus is reformator. After centuries of separate veneration from mortals, Lancea et Sanctum need to start following belief much more like mortals \u2013 or the questions will rise too much in daylight society. Even if he is not lifting Third Tradition of Timothy that banned worship with mortals - Iovinus is putting elements of Byzantine Rite to his black masses in Cisterns under Hagia Sophia, in Byzantium city. He is forcing old Roman natured Elders to speak in Greek, like Romanoi around them. He worries that next Plague can hit capitol because vampires stands too much from their kin and God will show his wrath on Constantinopole for breaking Masquerade.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Athanatoi</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>Viator \u2013 Dominus Noctis Imperator</b><br /> <br /> <b>Clan</b>: Ventrue<br /> <b>Covenant:</b> Athanatoi ( future Invictus )<br /> / Having Venture as Night Emperor maybe a clich\u00e9 \u2013 but they exists for the archetypical reasons. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> /<br /> <br /> <b>Jaromir \u2013 Slavic Strategos</b><br /> <br /> <b>Clan</b>: Gangrel<br /> <b>Covenant:</b> Athanatoi ( future Invictus )<br /> / Strategos are \u2018generals of Emperor in terrain\u2019. Jaromir is previous Slavic commander of military, now in the Byzantine army. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> /<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Omphalos</b><br /> <br /> <b>Horde</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>Hafgrim \u2013 Viking General</b><br /> <br /> <b>Clan</b>: Gangrel<br /> <b>Covenant:</b> ???<br /> Hafgrim is one of generals that lead next siege of Constantinople. He is also brutish vampire, surviving in the sun when need to lead his armies. Embraced against his will, he miss the daylight. He seeks Contagion as way for resurrecting himself in to sun light, once and for all.<br /> / Do not know what Covenants were in Viking vampires society, if any. Maybe Belial Brood? But it\u2019s not sure in 2E <b>VtR</b>, I think? /","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 11-01-2019, 08:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-01T23:37:58-07:00","id":1345400,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Vampires Government \u2013 Night Emperor, Patriarch and Prisci Council</b></span><br /> <br /> Kindred society of Constantinople is governed like that of mortal \u2013 just much more stable. When in living Empire, ruler can be change for complete stranger in one, two decades \u2013 undead are much more certain in their choices. Mostly because they are virtually immortal. If he is clever in his politics, new <i>Dominus Noctis Imperator</i> ( Great Night Imperator ) is chosen once in few centuries when previous one is going to Torpor, from Prisci Council \u2013 leaders of Clans in city, and by this, in Empire. New Imperator is appointing now <i>Stratoegoi</i> ( sing. <i>Strategos </i>) \u2013 generals in the field, to look over his matters for him in Empire, under sacred Oaths to him. All other them are watched if they making will of God by the<i> Patriarch of the Damned</i>, <i>Vicar of Longinus</i>, <i>Archbishop of Constantinople. </i>Sanctified Patriarch and Imperator rule almost as co-princes, with Imperator taking matters of world and Patriarch those of souls.<br /> <br /> Within city, Kindred are divided into <i>thema</i>, administrative groups (usually divided by lineage) with specific responsibilities to the Kindred government who gained specific rights in return, usually in regard to where they might haven and feed. The <i>Mystikoi</i>, a line of Gangrel monks, serve as scribes and historians, for example, and are given the right to feed from the city\u2019s monastic population.<br /> <br /> Nowadays rules of Imperator and Prisci Council ( 700-1000 AD ) is result of <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Plague_of_Justinian\" target=\"_blank\">Justinian Plague</a> of 541 ( with it\u2019s repeated resurgences till 750 AD ) \u2013 called centuries later Black Death. With as high as 40% mortality rate in Empire, it took many of humans supplies and networks of older Roman Elders \u2013 leading to their downfall or even Final Death. With humans dying en masse and normal dead returning to \u2018life\u2019 \u2013 Kindred needed change of rules. With old Patriarch lost in tumult and Prisci Council finally dead, vampires looked for new leaders. It came with <i>Ventranis</i> \u2013 previous barbarians hordes leader from West that became general in Days Emperor armies. He with few others Ancillae helped new appointed Patriarch Ivonius enforced order in Plague stricken Constantinopole. Following traditions of living Eastern Roman Empire, he was anointed Dominus Noctis Imperator by Ivonius \u2013 and start it\u2019s rules as King ( or rather, Emperor ) of Night in Reigning City. He appointed his helpers as Prisci that now advise him in ranks of Athanatoi. Researchers in Imperial Library whispers that they found legend about Imperator\u2019s name giver \u2013 Ven \u2013 being connected to stories of Troy and creation of Julii Clan of old\u2026<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Dominus Noctis Imperator \u2013 Ventranis</b></span><br /> <b>Clan: \u2018Ven\u2019 ( future Ventrue )</b><br /> <b>Covenant:</b> Athanatoi ( future Invictus )<br /> <b>Embraced: </b>482 CE ( same as birth of Emperor Justinian )<br /> <br /> Centuries ago, Ventranis was commander of one of next barbarian armies that lead siege on Constantinople. What was not known \u2013 he already was vampire of ancient noble and leaders Clan spread inside \u2018uncivilised\u2019 lands. Some rumours said he is related to Julii, somehow. His strategic mind and acumen lead him to become Day Emperors Justinian general, helping, in the end, to defend Byzantium. He hid his vampiric condition as \u2018foreign customs of his people\u2019 \u2013 and led small politics in Empire. Then came the Plague and everything changed. Without Prisci Council and with old Patriarch missing, there was chaos. Ventranis took matters in his own hands, helped new Archbishop Iovinus, collected willing and able to bring order with him in the City. It took half century, but they done it. They become next Prisci Council and in next 50 years, Ventranis is crowned first Dominus Noctis Imperator. ( Circa year 650 AD. )<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Patriarch of the Damned \u2013 Iovinus</b></span><br /> <b>Clan: Daeva</b><br /> <b>Covenant:</b> Ag\u00eda Lans ( gr. Lancea Sanctum )<br /> <b>Embraced: </b>532 CE ( Start of building Hagia Sophia )<br /> <br /> Iovinus was mesmerizing Roman priest of Greek heritage. He was observed by previous Patriarch, Alexander, from his teenage years. Vicar of Longinus even tried to romance and tempt young cleric \u2013 which he succeed. But only after Nike riots in 532 AD Alexander understood that he need a Child to take after him. When the Day Emperor in same year started building of Hagia Sophia, Alexander knew it was sign. On his 33rd birthdays, just like his Sire, Iovinus died to be reborn in Longinus. He only had 9 years of his undead existence when Alexander disappeared with first wave of Plague. Confused and unready to rule, he probably would lose the power \u2013 if not help from Ventranis. Together they lead order and stability \u2013 and controlled Plague in Constantinopole Kindred society. They\u2019re alliance lead domain to prosper \u2013 and let Patriarch to look over the matters of soul \u2013 so, Ivonius crowned Ventranis as Dominus Noctis Imperator.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Prisci Council</b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Gangrel Priscus \u2013 Vigilius</b></span><br /> <b>Clan</b>: Gangrel<br /> <b>Covenant:</b> Athanatoi ( future Invictus )<br /> <b>Embraced: </b>585 CE ( Slavs invasion of Constantinopole )<br /> <br /> Vigilius was one of defenders of City before Slavs. He died with name of the Christ on his mouth. And later awoken to the night. He was resurrected by one of \u2018barbarian demons\u2019. He slew his original pagan Sire and drove to the Legions of Damned knight order. However, seeing as Legion is too much theological fanatics and much less real army \u2013 he looked for inspirations. It came when Plague once more hit the Constantinople, and Ventranis gone to organise help and fight with returned dead. Vigilius joined future Imperator and advised to him creating more secular forces of knights to defend Queen of Cities, with Legions being less and less real force. Together, they started what would become Athnatoi, laying Oaths to new appointed Imperator of Night.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Mekhet Priscus \u2013 Eugenia</b></span><br /> <b>Clan</b>: Mekhet<br /> <b>Covenant:</b> Athanatoi ( future Invictus )<br /> <b>Embraced: </b>543 CE ( Justinian Plague )<br /> <br /> Eugenia was daughter of Byzantine noble. She could not go to Church run university, but learned all she could as independent Roman noblewomen. She devoured ancient scrolls and books on medicine and anatomy. If she was not women, she could become doctor. And then Plague came. She tried to fight it on streets. She tried to save her family when father brought sickness from the next military campaign. Finally, she did not save them - and she was dead. She awoke in the mass grave of Plague victims, from what she crawled up. Her Sire has prepared her and pointed her to save human and Kindred from Plague. And so she started to fight it, with all her knowledge and might. When Ventranis called for help, she gladly joined him. For the good of Empire \u2013 and it\u2019s people!<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Nosferatu Priscus \u2013 Skolikas ( Worm )</b></span><br /> <b>Clan</b>: Nosferatu<br /> <b>Covenant:</b> Athanatoi ( future Invictus )<br /> <b>Embraced: </b>541 CE ( Justinian Plague )<br /> <br /> Man called Skolikas was on of first victims of the Plague. The so called \u2018King of Beggars\u2019, he was finest fixer in the low strata of society. Of course, he was one of first to come in contact with sick and leppers. He was dying by days. Then his Mother give him choice of dying in pain \u2013 or too live forever with marks of disease. He choose later. He bears his Plague marks with pride \u2013 but he really want to end suffering of poor and outcast. He helped Ventranis \u2013 and now make sure that people on the low end of social ladder will also have voice. His voice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}